# Project: Money-event → RM call list engine (FDE intern assignment)

Goal: given a real Indian money event (IPO, acquisition, buyback, etc.), return a ranked list of
people a wealth-firm RM should call. Each person gets: name and role (as the source states them),
why they got money, a ₹ range with working shown, timing, confidence (kept separate from amount),
evidence links, and a 3–4 line RM brief.

HARD RULES — never break these:
1. Never invent a number, name, date, or regulation. Every figure comes from a source document
   (URL + page number) or is labelled ESTIMATE with the formula shown.
2. No hard-coding of specific companies, events, or people anywhere in code or prompts.
   The system will be tested live on an event nobody has seen.
3. Every LLM call goes through llm_call() in tools/llm.py, which logs cost.
   Never call a model SDK directly anywhere else.
4. Every network fetch goes through tools/fetch.py, which caches by URL + content hash.
5. Plain Python only. No agent frameworks. Use code instead of an LLM wherever the task is
   deterministic (parsing, arithmetic, matching, ranking).
6. Public data only. No LinkedIn. Don't scrape any site whose terms forbid it — if unsure,
   stop and ask me. Never collect phone numbers, personal emails, or home addresses.
7. If you're unsure about a fact or regulation (e.g., SEBI lock-in periods), do NOT fill it in
   from memory. Leave a clearly marked TODO saying what needs checking and where.
8. Keep functions small with a docstring each. I must be able to explain every line on a call.
9. After every task, end your reply with:
   (a) files changed, (b) assumptions you made, (c) what could break on an unseen event.
